{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/978886-inferno-2e-based-on-integrity","id":978886,"title":"Inferno 2E based on Integrity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T23:25:51-07:00","id":978886,"title":"Inferno 2E based on Integrity","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I initially presented </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">my</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> idea</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">s</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> for </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Inferno </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">rulebook update</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> to 2E in this topic. </span></span><span style=\"color:#0563C1\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-update-ideas</a></u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">This </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">discussion</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> is dedicated to a specific mechanics</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> I envision</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. If you do not agree with my assumptions - better to </span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">not</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> writing in it</span></span><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> and go somewhere else.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">You stayed? Okay, here is rough draft.</span> I took idea on Conditions and demon evolution from <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/\" target=\"_blank\">Charlaquin</a> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">post in original topic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2022 <i>Hearing Whispers </i>is a Persistent Condition that characters can gain instead of the normal Persistent Conditions for Dramatic Fauilre on Integrity Breaking Point if that Breaking Point played into their Vice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">\u2022 When a character with the <i>Hearing Whispers</i> Condition interacts with an ephemeral entity via the &quot;Interactions with Mortals&quot; or targets one with a supernatural power, there is a chance the mortal will lose the Condition and transfer it to the ephemeral entity.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Truth about Inferno</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Hell is dimension</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> outside of normal reality that mages describe as one of </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Lower </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Depths. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It\u2019s fueled by Sin \u2013 that in mechanics way is understood as Vice related Breaking Points</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, in which </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">act of </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Breaking Point marks \u2018</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">wickedness</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u2019</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. What\u2019s interesting, Breaking Points do not need to stir from humans Integrity \u2013 Humanity, </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Harmony or Wisdom are all good </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">food for Inferno demons.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Hell\u2019s servants feed on depraving and breaking people \u2013 supernatural or normal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Demons spread by Sin \u2013 when </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">someone is under Breaking Point based on Vice, he can start to hear Whisperer instead of other Dramatic </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Failure</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> effects</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> on roll.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> He </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Hearing Whisperer</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Condition</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> (see below)</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Diaboli</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are created by Ephemeral Beings interactions with Whisperers in others \u2013 or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">by some vile</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> ways of Inferno </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">entering our world </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">itself. Some say that really wicked ghosts can become </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Larvals </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">or that Sin polluted spirits can transform in to </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Immundi</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. Astral Realms are hosting </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Deceptors </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">from </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">g</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">oetia</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> of</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> those people that were infected with Whisperers. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">S</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">upposedly there are other methods </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">to corrupt </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">e</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">phemera</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">l beings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><i>Hearing Whisperer</i> ( </b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Persistent</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>, Vice )</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Your character is </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">hearing from time to time little voice in his head that leads him to commit sins. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">By listening to those </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">thoughts</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, she can rebuild her Willpower. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Character a</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">cts</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> as having second Vice decided when </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">acquiring this Condition. If Vice of Whisperer is the same as characters original, </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> her two Willpower points instead of one when </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">fulfilling</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> it. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">However, r</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">eal reward is in</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> breaking Integrity ( or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> equivalent ) in light of Sins \u2013 if character leads or is under Breaking Point based on the Vice of Whisperer, she regains number of Willpower points equal to cumulative negative penalties of the act.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Resolution:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Exorcism</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> of Whisperer. Mental </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">therapy</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Passing Whisperer to Ephemeral Being by contact with it</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> as per </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Mortal Interactions</i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> rules in </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>CoD</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b> Rulebook</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Beat:</b></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Your character chooses to </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">make act leading to Breaking Point based on Vice</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Confronting Ephemeral Being to pass the Whisperer to it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><b><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Inferno Demon Template</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">All Hell\u2019s demons are previous </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">E</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">phemeral </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">B</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">eings of other kinds \u2013 ghosts,</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> spirits or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">goetia</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">. ( Other </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">beings maybe also can be remade in to demons. ) Being then </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Inferno Demon Template on top of </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> original one, so </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Larvals</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> are still</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> and work under rules as</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> ghosts with Inferno Demon Template.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">New traits and rules for Inferno Demon:</span></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Being </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Vice trait, even if not having it previously.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> This Vice works as one for the ghosts.</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> If it did have other Vice before, Vice is switched to the one coming from transformation in to </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Hell\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">demon.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Being </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> new Influence based on </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Vice nature</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, called by demonologist as Key. This Key starts at Beings now Rank.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">If Being have Integrity</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> score</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> or </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">it\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">equivalent \u2013 she lose it in transformation.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Being new ways of generating Essence is making acts of Sin. She does not need to do it oneself. </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">It\u2019s even </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">advisable</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> that others should do those action in her place. If she makes acts of Sin, she </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> back her Rank in Essence. If she make </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>other </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">character </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">to do those</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">she also </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get\u2019s</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> bonus Essence</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> points</span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> in </span><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">number of negative penalties character got on her Breaking Points roll.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Here are some ideas I answered in previous topic on the problems with this mechanics...</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do not</i> want to strip demon of their previous templates advantages - mechanically ( and story-wise ) all demons were previous members of other ephemera - and they still should work as such. Demon ghosts were ghosts and still should have Integrity ( well, maybe without this one ), and surely Virtue and Vice. Demon spirits should not have Virtue, but Vice only in way of Key, not their own personality per se. Goetia <b>are</b> they own Virtue or Vice so should have those, paired with Key. In the nutshell - leave the basic ephemeral template alone, only <i><b>add</b></i> to it some Inferno corruption parts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably the heart of our contention - <b>I <i>do not </i>see need for separating those. </b>To me, <i>Breaking Point based on Vice is a Sin</i> - just see any big religion. Shooting to someone in anger - Wrath. Stealing something in needy - Greed. From my reading of <b>Inferno</b> book, <b>it's main idea is that Hell is feeding on breaking/corrupting characters.</b> It want's you to become more unstable, to lower Integrity. <i>Then</i> it can manipulate you, posses you.<br /> <br /> You really do not can make this one without involving somehow Breaking Points with Vice. Other way it will be 'I have Gluttonous character - I get to eat something big in time of work and now I'm posses by demon'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Whole idea of Inferno is that it wants to break your limits, more the better.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>( On monsters and their own Integrity in my take)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917052#post917052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they have their own Breaking Points that works with Vice induced idea so much better even. Mage risking his Wisdom on contacts with Inferno is really about not making so defenses to obvious, like sliping his important information in bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div>( On idea that murder is not Breaking Point for all characters )<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916379#post916379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where?<br /> <br /> Witnessing a murder \u20133<br /> Committing premeditated murder \u20135<br /> Killing in self-defense \u20134<br /> Killing by accident (car wreck, e.g.) \u20134<br /> Causing visible serious injury to a person \u20132<br /> <br /> But even when murdering is not Breaking Point for this character - murder-related demons just do not choose them as feeding sources. OR they rise the stakes - even your most hardened mercenary will roll on Breaking Point when he will massacre whole village.<br /> <br /> <b>What does it matter to the demon who is victim and who is perpetrator?</b> When being on scene of the act, demon just tap to the sources of Vice Essence through Breaking Point - and is the perpetrator losing Breaking Point or victim <i>does not have real meaning to it</i>. Essence is important to it. Who is providing it should not be anything more suitable than 'breaking someone more is giving me more Essence' or 'strategically, this person will make great Hells puppet'.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916379#post916379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inferno demons could be much more gourmets, looking for much more delicacy Essence - that is also suitable to both 1E portray and pop-culture idea of Hell demons. They look for particular taste, corrupting Integrity from Vice actions.<br /> <br /> Once again - I do not think that 'I must eat hot-dog' for Gluttons or 'I spend all day on couch' for Sloth characters are good Inferno demons targets - they do not sound enough... extreme. Adding need for Breaking Points to fulfill Vice action give us nice 'wickedness' feel to demons feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>On demons targeting children...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917860#post917860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add Demons who consume child innocence and attack children. As the servants of Demagogue in Little Fears including their kingdoms .</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917927#post917927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would nicely work as demons Essence feeding on Breaking Points 'innocents' have generally high Integrity levels.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"color:windowtext\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So what do you think about those rules? Did I miss something important?</span></span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T11:10:09-07:00","id":979159,"title":"","content":"Iike how you make Whisperers a persistant condition that can be past on to empherial entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:51:50-07:00","id":979215,"title":"","content":"Like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Generally, it works like this - You have Joe. Joe is normal human that has everyday job and everyman life. One day, when having really bad thoughts, he tried to kill himself. He did not succeed, but start to listen Whisperer. ( And getting <i>Hearing Whispers</i> ( Wrath ) Condition ). From now on, he hears from time to time voice from inside his head to beat or kill people, each time more and more extreme. First he beat defenseless homeless on the street. Then he killed his cat in fury. Then he killed stranger - because 'voices told him'. ( Each action is connected with Wrath and more and more demanding Breaking Point on characters Integrity. ) He start to suspect he is 'possessed or something', so he hit libraries and get a book on demon summoning and banishment. In reality, he 'banish' his own goetia of new Wrath ( see <i>Mortal Interaction</i> in <b>CoD Rulebook</b>, page 138 ) - and in this action, he both create it and forward his Whisperer, making goetia straight Inferno Deceptor. Joe is 'cured' of his <i>Hearing Whisper </i>Condition, but created new full fledged demon.<br /> <br /> If Joe would want to 'pact' with some concept spirit, because he mixed spells or lore, he would then change normal spirit into Immundi.<br /> <br /> What's even more ironic, each try on Joe's getting rid of Whisperer makes proper demon - and this demon can try to posses him once more, if he has Possession Manifestation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Crutial here are <i>Mortal Interaction</i> rules from <b>CoD Rulebook</b> - and those are, basically, summon or abjure ephemeral beings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2016, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}